<article class="env-lemma" id="09XB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09XB">Lemma <span data-tag="09XB">85.25.6</span>.</a> Let $U$ be a simplicial object of $\textit{LC}$ and let $a : U \to X$ be an augmentation. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian sheaf on $X$. Let $\mathcal{F}_ n$ be the pullback to $U_ n$. If $U$ is a proper hypercovering of $X$, then there exists a canonical spectral sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_1^{p, q} = H^ q(U_ p, \mathcal{F}_ p)  \]
</div>
  <p> converging to $H^{p + q}(X, \mathcal{F})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate consequence of Lemmas <a href="/tag/09XC" data-tag="09XC">85.25.4</a> and <a href="/tag/09W6" data-tag="09W6">85.2.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>